gI have been notified in criminal proceedings.A new chapterI am buying, selling or renting a property.A noticeI have received a letter from the Tax Authority.A change of directionI have a problem with my bank or with debt.Different situations. The same personal commitment.Calm, with a clear plan.A proceedingFirst, understand.Then, respond.We explain what the notice means, which deadlines apply and what options you have. We prepare the response with you, discreetly.NoticesDefenceDeadlinesExplore Criminal LawA solid basis for deciding.A new chapterMake roomfor what comes next.We check documents, charges and licences before you sign, and see the transaction through to registration.Preliminary contractDeed of saleLeasingExplore Real Estate LawA fresh perspective on the way forward.A noticeFind clarity.Then move forward.We analyse the assessment and explain whether to pay, object or appeal, always within the deadline.Income taxObjectionAppealExplore Tax LawAmbition, with a clear foundation.A change of directionRegain your balance.Step by step.We read the contract with you, assess the room to negotiate and, if needed, defend your interests in court.CreditRestructuringNegotiationExplore Banking & Finance LawA proceedingI have been notified in criminal proceedings.First, understand. Then, respond.We explain what the notice means, which deadlines apply and what options you have. We prepare the response with you, discreetly.Explore Criminal LawA new chapterI am buying, selling or renting a property.Make room for what comes next.We check documents, charges and licences before you sign, and see the transaction through to registration.Explore Real Estate LawA noticeI have received a letter from the Tax Authority.Find clarity. Then move forward.We analyse the assessment and explain whether to pay, object or appeal, always within the deadline.Explore Tax LawA change of directionI have a problem with my bank or with debt.Regain your balance. Step by step.We read the contract with you, assess the room to negotiate and, if needed, defend your interests in court.Explore Banking & Finance LawHow we workUnderstand first.Act with clarity.Good counsel is a conversation. This is how we turn yours into a plan.01ListenFirst, your perspective.We begin with your situation, your priorities and what a good outcome would mean to you.02ClarifyA plan you understand.Your options, the trade-offs and the next steps, explained clearly before we move forward.03ActStrategy, with rigour.We carry out the plan with technical rigour and keep you informed at every important decision.04Stay closeBeyond the immediate.A continuing conversation about your priorities and the decisions still ahead.Every step, in partnership.Start by telling us about your situationOur peoplePeople you knowby name.A close-knit team with more than twenty years of practice in Aveiro and Oliveira de Frades.José Carreto LagesFounding PartnerCriminal Law · Tax LawJoão Carlos LagesPartner and Managing DirectorReal Estate Law · Banking & Finance LawCatarina Pereira CarvalhoPartner and Managing DirectorReal Estate LawMeet the teamCase studiesOur work,in real cases.Criminal LawIllustrative exampleAcquittal in a computer fraud caseA client accused of unlawful access to computer systems, with a civil compensation claim attached.OutcomeAcquittal and dismissal of the civil claim.Real Estate LawIllustrative exampleRecovering a property in insolvency proceedingsA company's property wrongly attached in enforcement proceedings.OutcomeThe attachment was lifted and the property returned to the client's assets.Tax LawIllustrative exampleChallenging an additional income tax assessmentAn individual facing an additional income tax assessment for allegedly undeclared income.OutcomeThe assessment was cancelled in full at the administrative stage.See all case studiesTestimonialsIn the wordsof those who trusted us.Illustrative example“They explained everything clearly from day one. I always knew where I stood and what ca